      "problem": "Find the solution to the equation ${e}^{8x}=\\sqrt{5}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{8x} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{8x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{5}) \\\\ 8x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{1/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.101\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
